{"scenario":"bad-deploy","description":"payment v2.4.1 ships a card tokenizer bug (+ an unrelated catalog deploy as a red herring)","mode":"graph","recorded_at":"2026-10-18 04:02","duration":77.42,"agent":{"duration_s":44.2,"tool_calls":10,"cost_usd":0.1370208,"input_tokens":105668,"output_tokens":2653,"report":"## Resolved INC-043 (SEV2): frontend error spike\n\nA bad payment deploy caused the frontend errors. I rolled payment back and frontend recovered; the incident was open for about 0.4 min.\n\n**Root cause:** payment v2.4.1, deployed in change chg-aa57b272 (saved-card tokenization refactor, by riya). It went out 8s before the alert. It crashes on saved cards that have no card number: `TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not subscriptable` at `card_tokenizer.py:88`. About 67% of payment requests failed (18 of 27).\n\n**Evidence path:**\n`frontend` (32% errors, all from its dependencies) \u2192 `checkout` (50% errors, all from its dependencies) \u2192 `payment` (failing inside payment itself; its own dependencies are healthy) \u2192 **chg-aa57b272**\n- **Logs:** all 24 recent payment log entries were the same tokenizer exception, from v2.4.1.\n- **Past incident:** INC-031 was the same kind of bug, a missing null check on saved cards in payment's card tokenizer. A rollback fixed it then too.\n- **Ruled out:** the catalog v3.1.0 deploy, made 18s before the alert, because catalog stayed healthy at 0% errors. fraud-check, inventory and notify were also healthy with no recent changes.\n\n**Action taken (1 of the 3 allowed):** I ran `rollback_service payment` as a dry run, which planned v2.4.1 \u2192 v2.4.0 and reverted exactly chg-aa57b272. Then I ran it for real; the new deploy is chg-4da24ae1.\n\n**Verification:** frontend dropped to 5.1% errors (degraded) at about 4s, then 0% (healthy) at 7s and 10s. p95 latency stayed around 112ms, the same as during the incident, so latency was never the problem.\n\n**Paged:** riya (on-call for the payments team, #team-payments). There's no webhook configured, so the page is only recorded in the incident graph and nobody was actually alerted. They were asked to add the null check and a regression test before shipping v2.4.1 again.\n\nThe incident is resolved with chg-aa57b272 recorded as the root cause, so similar incidents will show up in future searches.","start_t":19.88,"end_t":64.97},"events":[{"t":0.06,"kind":"start","text":"healthy baseline"},{"t":3.1,"kind":"inject","text":"payment v2.4.1 ships a card tokenizer bug (+ an unrelated catalog deploy as a red herring)"},{"t":19.88,"kind":"alert","text":"ALERT frontend error rate 32%, p95 108ms"},{"t":19.88,"kind":"agent","text":"headless agent started (graph mode)"},{"t":64.97,"kind":"done","text":"agent finished"}],"steps":[{"t":22.7,"n":1,"tool":"get_service_health","note":"checked health of all services","targets":["Service:checkout","Service:frontend","Service:payment"]},{"t":22.76,"n":2,"tool":"rank_suspects","note":"top suspect payment (score 0.978) via path frontend -> checkout -> payment","targets":["Service:catalog","Service:checkout","Service:frontend","Service:payment","Change:chg-2babf1fc","Change:chg-aa57b272"]},{"t":24.29,"n":3,"tool":"get_logs","note":"read 24 log entries of payment","targets":["Service:payment"]},{"t":24.73,"n":4,"tool":"find_similar_incidents","note":"3 similar past incidents, best INC-031","targets":["Incident:INC-019","Incident:INC-027","Incident:INC-031"]},{"t":28.41,"n":5,"tool":"open_incident","note":"INC-043: Frontend errors: payment v2.4.1 card tokenizer crash","targets":["Incident:INC-043"]},{"t":30.96,"n":6,"tool":"get_blast_radius","note":"blast radius of payment: 2 upstream, 1 downstream","targets":["Service:checkout","Service:fraud-check","Service:frontend","Service:payment"]},{"t":30.97,"n":7,"tool":"rollback_service","note":"DRY RUN rollback payment v2.4.1 -> v2.4.0","targets":["Service:payment","Change:chg-aa57b272"]},{"t":33.67,"n":8,"tool":"get_blast_radius","note":"blast radius of payment: 